# leaf.cyr — fixture for v5.9.34 PP comment-quote regression.
#
# Documents JSON escape syntax inside backticks. The literal byte
# sequence `\"` (backtick-backslash-quote-backtick) inside a
# comment was the trigger for vyakarana 1.0.2's include-graph
# build break under cyrius v5.8.40 .. v5.9.33: the backslash
# was a no-op outside a string and the unescaped `"` toggled
# `in_string=1`, leaving every subsequent include directive
# unexpanded.
#
# Quote-bearing comment line below stays single-source-of-truth:
# references inside strings: `\\`, `\"`,
# `\n`, `\t`. That's enough for grammar files; we don't need
# `\u` (Unicode escape) in 1.0.

fn _leaf_value() { return 7; }
